WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.446
Recycled inputs change. A product still has a job to do. ReMatter starts with what you have,

00:00:06.446 --> 00:00:12.891
what varies, and the result you need. This is a software demonstration using synthetic readings, not a

00:00:12.891 --> 00:00:19.337
tested recycled material. The user chooses the product. Here, a contained ballast module needs both a mass

00:00:19.337 --> 00:00:21.232
range and a balance-point range.

00:00:21.232 --> 00:00:28.052
Meta proposes practical routes from this same case. Instead of rejecting a variable core, this route keeps

00:00:28.052 --> 00:00:34.872
it contained and adds two sealed trim locations. These are engineering proposals, not verified material recipes. The

00:00:34.872 --> 00:00:40.488
case and targets carry into the calculation; I do not select the material again.

00:00:40.488 --> 00:00:46.345
Here is the trap in checking weight alone. The assembly is nine hundred and fifty grams, with

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:52.203
a stated weighing bound. Adding fifty grams on the left meets the mass target, but the balance

00:00:52.203 --> 00:00:58.060
point still misses. The joint tool checks both targets, both trim locations, the available amounts, and the

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:03.917
entered uncertainty bounds. Rounded commands are checked again. The result is add one hundred and four grams

00:01:03.917 --> 00:01:09.085
on the left and remove fifty-four on the right. Both ranges fit within this simulation.

00:01:09.085 --> 00:01:15.549
This is a fresh Meta request. Meta calls the engineering tool and explains the checked action. The

00:01:15.549 --> 00:01:22.013
downloadable record retains the actual calculation, inputs, and model turns. The model does not invent a density

00:01:22.013 --> 00:01:28.477
or transfer a public plastic study into my mix. The diagram shows where the trim belongs; it

00:01:28.477 --> 00:01:30.379
is not a manufacturing drawing.

00:01:30.379 --> 00:01:36.473
Now consider another synthetic observation of the same product. The mass is already one kilogram, but the

00:01:36.473 --> 00:01:42.568
balance point is five millimetres off centre. The old balance reading and result clear automatically. I enter

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:48.663
the matching new balance reading. Meta runs the joint check again. This time the action is add

00:01:48.663 --> 00:01:54.757
forty-two grams on the left and remove forty-two on the right. Total nominal mass stays the same

00:01:54.757 --> 00:01:59.776
while the balance moves. The downloadable record keeps this observation and its actual calculation.

00:01:59.776 --> 00:02:06.721
What have we proved? A working software loop from a shared case to an adjustment amount and

00:02:06.721 --> 00:02:13.665
location, then a revised action from a new observation. We have not proved physical performance or future-batch

00:02:13.665 --> 00:02:20.610
consistency. Simpler baselines matched the arithmetic, and a parser matched note extraction faster. ReMatter connects engineering proposals,

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:27.554
checked calculations and a clear next action. Retention, durability and tipping safety still need their own tests.
